{
  "_note": [
    "THE COMPATIBLE-SET HISTORY, AS DATA. One row per compatible set this policy has",
    "committed that approved any peer revision, oldest first (pilot-1 approved none); the",
    "last row IS the set release/policy.json approves, and committed-policy.test.mjs holds",
    "the two equal. Nothing here is read by the release gate: it is evidence for the",
    "committed-policy tests, which replay every row through the real decision rule.",
    "",
    "A ROW records what the set approved (`approved`, one commit per peer); the facts of",
    "each receipt it approved FIRST (`receipts`, checked against release/peers/ byte for",
    "byte); the backend serving note its decisions printed (`backendServingReason`); the",
    "owner-prerequisite states it was committed under (`ownerStates`); what its refresh",
    "moved and removed; the revisions reviewed with it but never approved (`notApproved`);",
    "`refused`, the decisions taken under the PREVIOUS set that prompted this refresh; and",
    "`decisions`, those taken under this set. Each decision is the reasons it refused",
    "beyond its owner state's awaiting list (`unexpected`) and its digest. `evidence` says",
    "what it is: `recorded` (a readiness run bound it, or logged its reasons when the digest",
    "is null), `constructed` or `synthetic` (computed from the rule; no run recorded it",
    "under that set). A recorded digest is never replaced by a computed one.",
    "",
    "A REFRESH APPENDS ONE ROW and edits no other. Every receipt under release/peers/ is",
    "declared here, and a retained receipt is never deleted. Receipts are produced by",
    "`node release/cli.mjs peer-receipt` at the exact commit and re-derived independently",
    "before they are approved; release/README.md (\"Refreshing the compatible set\") gives",
    "the procedure and records each refresh's review.",
    "",
    "AN OWNER-STATE CHANGE under an unchanged set id (R-1; the 2026-10-27 source-protection",
    "record) adds one `ownerStates` entry and extends the last row's `ownerStates` and",
    "`decisions`. A state's overrides are applied over the committed policy, so every state",
    "names each prerequisite status an owner-state change has moved, earlier states included."
  ],
  "schema": "dinify.release.compatible-set-history/1",
  "backendServingReasons": {
    "no-identity-published": "the backend publishes no served-revision identity (B3); which backend revision is live cannot be observed, and an operator statement is not accepted as serving evidence",
    "no-loaded-runtime-identity": "no verified loaded-runtime identity of the backend is available (B3): its source carries a release-identity endpoint and a staged installer, but the installer is not active, the legacy deploy-uat.yml still serves, and by that source a process the legacy deploy starts answers the endpoint as unavailable; which backend revision is live therefore cannot be observed, and an operator statement is not accepted as serving evidence"
  },
